{
 "encounter_id": "00661",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello again, doctor. I know it's only a cough, but it's been going on for three weeks now and it's driving me round the bend."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Not just a cough if it's driven you in. Tell me what it's like."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Dry, tickly, mostly. It starts as soon as I lie down at night, and I'm getting no sleep. Oh, and sometimes I cough so hard I feel sick."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And it began with a cold?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A bad cold, yes, three weeks ago. The cold went, but the cough stayed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever, or coughing up blood?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No fever, no blood. Nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Weight loss, sweats at night, anything of that kind?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, I've actually put on a bit of weight, sadly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Let's check what you take regularly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The ramipril, 5 mg once a day, for my blood pressure, and metformin, 500 mg twice a day. That's it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And remind me of your other conditions, apart from the blood pressure."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've got type 2 diabetes, and I had asthma as a child, but I grew out of it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I see. Let me check your temperature, pulse and oxygen. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Temperature 36.7, pulse 76, oxygen 98 percent.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All fine, I suppose. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All fine. Breathe in and out for me, normally. I'm listening to your chest.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is it clear? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Your chest is clear, no crackles and no wheeze. Open wide. Your throat is a bit red at the back.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So what's wrong with me? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "After a cold, it's common for the airways to stay twitchy for weeks, so I think this is most likely a post-viral cough."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. How long will it go on? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It can last up to eight weeks. But there's one other thing. Ramipril, your blood pressure tablet, can itself cause a dry, tickly cough in some people, so I can't rule out a side effect of the ramipril."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Oh! I never thought of that. I've been on it for years. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Sometimes it starts late. I wouldn't stop it yet, but let's keep it in mind. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What do we do now? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Because it's been three weeks, I'd like to do a chest X-ray, to be sure there's nothing in the lungs. And a spirometry test to check your airways."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "And bloods? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, a blood test as well, to check your blood count and sugar control while we're at it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. And what do I do about the cough? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Honey and warm water at night can soothe the throat, and propping up on an extra pillow helps with lying down."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll try the honey. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, with the results, and we'll decide about the ramipril then."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three weeks. Thanks, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
